{"translation-revision-date":"+0000","generator":"WP-CLI\/2.12.0","source":"assets\/js\/app.js","domain":"messages","locale_data":{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","lang":"zh_CN","plural-forms":"nplurals=1; plural=0;"},"Item":[""],"%s restored for them":[""],"Signed out everywhere":[""],"Sign this user out of all sessions?":[""],"Session signed out":[""],"User updated":[""],"language pack installed":[""],"Delete user":[""],"Deleting a user asks what happens to their content first.":[""],"Danger zone":[""],"Sign out everywhere":[""],"Sign out":[""],"signed in":[""],"No active sessions.":[""],"Sessions":[""],"Restore":[""],"Items this user chose to hide from their own Minimal. Restoring brings one back for them.":[""],"Hidden for them":[""],"The WordPress admin bar on the front end while they are signed in.":[""],"Show toolbar when viewing the site":[""],"After sign-in they land in Minimal. Full wp-admin stays available.":[""],"Minimal is their default admin":[""],"Color scheme":[""],"Set their Minimal palette now so it looks right before their first sign-in. Light or dark mode stays a device preference each person controls themselves.":[""],"what this user sees":[""],"Appearance":[""],"Bio":[""],"Website":[""],"Last name":[""],"First name":[""],"author boxes & archives":[""],"Public profile":[""],"Save changes":[""],"Generate":[""],"New password (leave blank to keep)":[""],"Language":[""],"Role":[""],"Email":[""],"Display name":[""],"Loading user\u2026":[""],"Could not load this user.":[""],"No guide found.":[""],"Value copied":[""],"Copied (truncated value)":[""],"Everything Minimal writes is native WordPress: real block markup, core options, core users. Deactivate the plugin and nothing is lost. Plugins extend Minimal with one PHP filter, as plain data, which is why nothing here can nag you.":[""]," and hand your AI agent a revocable credential to do the fiddly work over the REST API.":[""],"Your profile \u2192 AI Access":[""],"Minimal surfaces the settings people change day to day; the long tail stays in wp-admin on purpose. For plugin configuration Minimal doesn't rebuild, open":[""],"Deliberately minimal":[""],"Anything a plugin adds here can be hidden for you alone: right-click its sidebar entry or block-library heading and choose Hide. Everything hidden is listed on Your profile, where one click restores it.":[""],"Make it yours":[""],"The least discoverable thing in Minimal, so here it is in writing: rows in Content and Media, comments, the theme button, plugin entries in the sidebar and group headings in the block library all have right-click menus. When in doubt, try a right-click.":[""],"Right-click almost anything":[""],", then start typing a view, a post or a command.":[""],"The sidebar has three groups: Workspace (the daily material), Tools (what your plugins add) and Manage (the site itself). The fastest way anywhere is the command palette:":[""],"Getting around":[""],"A calm, fast surface for the work you do every day: writing, moderating, uploading, and keeping an eye on the site. Classic wp-admin stays fully available, one click away.":[""],"Minimal is a reimagined WordPress admin.":[""],"Loading the guide\u2026":[""],"User guide":[""],"View the full changelog with screenshots on FeiCode repository":[""],"Open the user guide":[""],"Browse database (read-only)":[""],"Updating %s plugin\u2026":[""],"Pattern insert failed: ":[""],"Pattern unavailable":[""],"Synced":[""],"Your patterns":[""],"(untitled pattern)":[""],"This is a synced pattern \u2014 saving changes here updates every post and page that uses it.":[""],"Status":[""],"Edit via \u2699 or the block editor":[""],"Styled block: edit text via \u2699":[""],"Could not reach the server. Please try again.":[""],"The key was not accepted.":[""],"Key saved and verified":[""],"Turn off":[""],"Showing the first %1$s of %2$s.":[""],"Copy":[""],"This table has no indexes.":[""],"Cardinality":[""],"Unique":[""],"Index":[""],"Indexes":[""],"No":[""],"Yes":[""],"Ext